{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfun2aYT7KBvzYS9i9XzC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"As far as I know, Cloudflare Workflows has **no built-in per-workflow concurrency setting** in `wrangler.toml`/`wrangler.jsonc`. The only cap is the account-level platform limit on concurrently running instances. Extra instances are queued rather than rejected. Check the current Workflows \"Limits\" docs for the exact number, since it has changed over time.\n\nTo enforce your own cap, throttle where instances are created:\n\n- **Queue (simplest):** Send work to a Cloudflare Queue. Have the consumer call `env.MY_WORKFLOW.create()`, and set `max_concurrency` (and `max_batch_size`) on the consumer.\n  - This only limits how fast instances *start*, not how many are *running*. For a true cap, have the consumer check how many instances are running, or wait on them, before creating more.\n- **Durable Object semaphore (strict cap):** A single Durable Object tracks active instances. A workflow acquires a slot before its main work, either at creation or in a first `step.do`, and releases it in a final step. If no slot is free, it waits with `step.sleep` and retries.\n\nIf a native limit option has been added recently, it would be in the Workflows configuration docs, so check those before building your own."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2249,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2249},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"54bc7c5c-16f0-4e07-a4a0-e6b64c3c03c2","uuid":"7d1b31d1-db24-4f5e-b990-a3c40580f55e","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:56:54.881Z","request_id":"req_011Cfun2aKJWqc7coAwgCFso"}
